<!--meta {"lead": "The top bar is the same on every HairPop screen: the brand, the four primary destinations, unread updates and Maya's account. It is how people move between styles, braiders and their appointments.", "description": "Sticky app header with brand, primary navigation, updates count, account link and a phone menu button.", "pills": ["<code>&lt;header&gt;</code> + <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>", "Status: stable"], "variants": "default (desktop), compact with menu button (phone), menu open", "states": "link default, hover, focus, active, current; menu collapsed, expanded", "sources": ["pages/style-gallery/default", "pages/matching-braiders/default", "pages/my-appointments/default", "pages/help/default"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Every product screen starts with the top bar inside <code>.product-shell</code>. It holds exactly what a customer needs from anywhere: the HairPop brand (back to the style gallery), the primary navigation, the <b>Updates</b> link with an unread count, and the account link with Maya's first name. Keep page-specific actions out of it; they belong in the <a href="page-header.html">page header</a>.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Desktop and tablet</b> (from 768px) show the brand, the four primary links (Styles, Braiders, Appointments, Help), then Updates and the account link on the right.</li>
    <li><b>Phones</b> (below 768px) collapse the four links behind a menu button so every destination is still one tap away.</li>
    <li>Use <a href="sidebar-navigation.html">sidebar navigation</a> instead only for a future tool with more than six destinations, such as a braider studio.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure" style="padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-4);">
      <div class="ds-frame" style="width: 100%; margin: 0;">
        <header class="topbar"><a class="topbar__brand" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">{{icon:sparkle}}HairPop</a><nav class="topbar__nav" aria-label="Primary, anatomy example"><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html" aria-current="page">Styles</a><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/matching-braiders/default.html">Braiders</a></nav><span class="topbar__spacer"></span><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/notification-center/default.html">Updates <span class="badge badge--count">2</span><span class="visually-hidden">, 2 unread</span></a><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/account-settings/default.html">Maya</a></header>
      </div>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 10%; top: 18%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 36%; top: 18%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 74%; top: 18%;" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 89%; top: 18%;" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 52%; top: 80%;" aria-hidden="true">5</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Brand</b><small>Sparkle icon + "HairPop" in <code>--text-h4</code>, <code>--color-fg-accent</code>; links to the style gallery.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Primary navigation</b><small><code>&lt;nav aria-label="Primary"&gt;</code> of nav links, 44px tall; the current page uses <code>aria-current="page"</code>.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Updates</b><small>Account link with a count <a href="badge.html">badge</a>; the count is part of the visible name.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Account</b><small>The customer's first name; links to account settings.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Container</b><small>56px (<code>--layout-topbar-height</code>), surface background, bottom hairline, sticky at <code>--z-sticky</code>, side padding <code>--layout-margin</code>.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  <p>One component, two arrangements decided by the viewport, plus the open menu on phones.</p>
  <h3>Default (768px and wider)</h3>
  {{example:[stack]Brand, four primary links, then Updates and the account on the right. This frame follows your window width.}}
<div class="ds-frame" style="margin: 0;"><header class="topbar"><a class="topbar__brand" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">{{icon:sparkle}}HairPop</a><nav class="topbar__nav" id="topbar-nav-default" aria-label="Primary, default example"><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html" aria-current="page">Styles</a><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/matching-braiders/default.html">Braiders</a><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/my-appointments/default.html">Appointments</a><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/help/default.html">Help</a></nav><span class="topbar__spacer"></span><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/notification-center/default.html">Updates <span class="badge badge--count">2</span><span class="visually-hidden">, 2 unread</span></a><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon topbar__menu" type="button" aria-label="Menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="topbar-nav-default">{{icon:menu}}</button><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/account-settings/default.html">Maya</a></header></div>
  {{/example}}
  <h3>Compact with menu open (phones)</h3>
  <p>Below 768px the primary links hide and the menu button appears. Opening it reveals the same four links, in the same order, directly under the bar; the current page stays marked.</p>
  {{example:[stack]Shown at phone width. The panel is the same <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>, revealed by the button; it pushes content down rather than covering it.}}
<div class="ds-frame ds-phone" style="margin: 0;"><div class="topbar" style="position: static;"><a class="topbar__brand" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">{{icon:sparkle}}HairPop</a><span class="topbar__spacer"></span><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/notification-center/default.html">Updates <span class="badge badge--count">2</span><span class="visually-hidden">, 2 unread</span></a><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="Menu" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="topbar-nav-phone">{{icon:close}}</button></div><nav id="topbar-nav-phone" class="stack stack--sm" style="padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4) var(--space-4); background: var(--color-bg-surface); border-bottom: var(--border-width-hairline) solid var(--color-border-default);" aria-label="Primary, phone example"><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">Styles</a><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/matching-braiders/default.html">Braiders</a><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/my-appointments/default.html" aria-current="page">Appointments</a><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/help/default.html">Help</a><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/account-settings/default.html">Maya · account</a></nav></div>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="The top bar has one height (56px, --layout-topbar-height) at every breakpoint; only its contents change."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>The bar itself has no states; its links and menu button do. Pointer and focus states are forced with <code>data-state</code>; real pages use <code>:hover</code>, <code>:focus-visible</code>, <code>aria-current</code> and <code>aria-expanded</code>.</p>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Element</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Hover</th><th scope="col">Focus</th><th scope="col">Active</th><th scope="col">Current / expanded</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Nav link</th><td><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/matching-braiders/default.html">Braiders</a></td><td><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/matching-braiders/default.html" data-state="hover">Braiders</a></td><td><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/matching-braiders/default.html" data-state="focus">Braiders</a></td><td><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/matching-braiders/default.html" data-state="hover">Braiders</a></td><td><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/matching-braiders/default.html" aria-current="page">Braiders</a></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Brand</th><td><a class="topbar__brand" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">{{icon:sparkle}}HairPop</a></td><td><a class="topbar__brand" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html" style="color: var(--color-fg-link-hover);">{{icon:sparkle}}HairPop</a></td><td><a class="topbar__brand" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html" data-state="focus">{{icon:sparkle}}HairPop</a></td><td><a class="topbar__brand" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html" style="color: var(--color-fg-link-hover);">{{icon:sparkle}}HairPop</a></td><td>–</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Account link</th><td><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/account-settings/default.html">Maya</a></td><td><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/account-settings/default.html" data-state="hover">Maya</a></td><td><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/account-settings/default.html" data-state="focus">Maya</a></td><td><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/account-settings/default.html" data-state="active">Maya</a></td><td>–</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Menu button</th><td><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="Menu" aria-expanded="false">{{icon:menu}}</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="Menu" aria-expanded="false" data-state="hover">{{icon:menu}}</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="Menu" aria-expanded="false" data-state="focus">{{icon:menu}}</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="Menu" aria-expanded="false" data-state="active">{{icon:menu}}</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="Menu" aria-expanded="true">{{icon:close}}</button></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>Nav links have no separate pressed look: the active (pointer down) state keeps the hover background. Navigation links are never disabled; a destination the customer cannot use (for example Appointments while signed out) still links, and the destination explains why.</p>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes:stack}}<div class="topbar" style="position: static; padding-inline: var(--space-4); flex-wrap: wrap;"><span class="topbar__brand">{{icon:sparkle}}HairPop</span><a class="nav-link" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html" aria-current="page">Styles</a><span class="topbar__spacer"></span><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/notification-center/default.html">Updates <span class="badge badge--count">2</span><span class="visually-hidden">, 2 unread</span></a></div>{{/themes}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Below 768px</b> (<code>--layout-breakpoint-md</code>): <code>.topbar__nav</code> hides and <code>.topbar__menu</code> shows. The menu button controls the nav panel with <code>aria-expanded</code> + <code>aria-controls</code>. The account link drops to <code>--font-size-sm</code>.</li>
    <li><b>From 768px</b>: the four links show inline after the brand and the menu button hides. Links never wrap to a second row; at 768px all four fit with the brand, Updates and Maya.</li>
    <li>The bar stays 56px tall and sticky at every width. <code>scroll-padding-top</code> on <code>html</code> equals the bar height plus <code>--space-4</code>, so focused or anchored content is never hidden behind it (WCAG 2.4.11).</li>
    <li>Side padding follows <code>--layout-margin</code> (16 → 32 → 48px), so the brand lines up with the page content below.</li>
    <li>At 320px the brand, Updates with its count and the menu button still fit; the account link moves into the menu panel.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>The bar reads <code>--topbar-bg</code> (aliasing <code>--color-bg-surface</code>) and <code>--color-border-default</code>; links read the nav-link tokens. Override <code>--topbar-bg</code> for a campaign or partner theme, never the rules. In the dark theme the surface becomes grey 900 over the grey 950 canvas so the bar still reads as a layer, the brand and current link turn plum 300, and the current-link background becomes plum 950.</p>
  <pre><code>/* A studio sub-brand with a sunken bar */
.studio .topbar { --topbar-bg: var(--color-bg-surface-sunken); }</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p><code>&lt;header class="topbar"&gt;</code> is the page's banner landmark; the links sit in <code>&lt;nav aria-label="Primary"&gt;</code>. The phone menu follows the <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/disclosure/">APG Disclosure</a> pattern: a <code>&lt;button aria-expanded aria-controls="primary-nav"&gt;</code> that shows the same <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>. It is not an ARIA <code>menu</code>; links stay plain links in Tab order.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>After the skip link: brand, primary links in order, Updates, menu button (phones), account.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd></td><td>Follows a link.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd>, <kbd>Space</kbd></td><td>On the menu button: opens or closes the nav panel and toggles <code>aria-expanded</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Esc</kbd></td><td>With the panel open: closes it and returns focus to the menu button.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>The shared 2px plum ring with 2px offset. Opening the phone menu leaves focus on the button (the panel follows it in DOM order); choosing a link navigates, and the new page starts focus at the skip link.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>The nav is labelled "Primary" (use a different label for any second nav on the page). The current page uses <code>aria-current="page"</code>, never colour alone. The Updates link's accessible name must contain its visible text: "Updates" + count + visually hidden ", 2 unread" reads "Updates 2, 2 unread". Do not put a second <code>aria-label</code> on the badge inside the link. The menu button is labelled "Menu" and states its expansion.</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Nav link on bar|--color-fg-muted|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Current link on its background|--color-fg-accent|--color-accent-subtle|4.5}}
    {{pair:Hovered link|--color-fg-default|--color-bg-subtle|4.5}}
    {{pair:Brand on bar|--color-fg-accent|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Unread count|--color-fg-on-danger|--color-danger-solid|4.5}}
    {{pair:Focus ring on bar|--color-focus-ring|--color-bg-surface|3}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>Link background and colour change over <code>--duration-fast</code>. The phone panel appears without a slide; under reduced motion every transition is instant because the tokens zero the durations.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>Nav links, the brand and the account links are 44px tall (<code>--target-comfortable</code>); the menu button is 40px square with at least 12px to its neighbours.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Primary links are one-word nouns, in this order everywhere: Styles, Braiders, Appointments, Help.</li>
    <li>The account link shows the customer's first name ("Maya"); when signed out it reads "Sign in".</li>
    <li>"Updates" shows the unread count only when it is above zero; above 99 it shows "99+" with the full number in the hidden text.</li>
    <li>The brand is the word "HairPop" with the sparkle icon; never a tagline in the bar.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="topbar" style="position: static; width: 100%;"><span class="topbar__brand">{{icon:sparkle}}HairPop</span><span class="topbar__spacer"></span><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="Menu" aria-expanded="false">{{icon:menu}}</button></div></div><figcaption>On phones, keep every destination reachable behind a labelled menu button.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="topbar" style="position: static; width: 100%;"><span class="topbar__brand">✦ HairPop</span><span class="topbar__spacer"></span><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/account-settings/default.html">Maya</a></div></div><figcaption>Hide the links below 768px with no menu, as the mocks do: Braiders, Appointments and Help become unreachable on phones.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/notification-center/default.html">Updates <span class="badge badge--count">2</span><span class="visually-hidden">, 2 unread</span></a></div><figcaption>The accessible name starts with the visible word: "Updates 2, 2 unread".</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><a class="account-link" href="../../mocks/pages/notification-center/default.html" aria-label="Notifications, 2 unread">Updates <span class="badge badge--count">2</span></a></div><figcaption>Label "Updates" as "Notifications" for screen readers. Voice users saying "click Updates" get no match (WCAG 2.5.3).</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Bar background|--color-bg-surface}}
      {{tok:Bottom edge|--color-border-default}}
      {{tok:Brand|--color-fg-accent}}
      {{tok:Nav link label|--color-fg-muted}}
      {{tok:Nav link hover background|--color-bg-subtle}}
      {{tok:Current link background|--color-accent-subtle}}
      {{tok:Account link|--color-fg-default}}
      {{tok:Unread count|--color-danger-solid}}
      {{tok:Height|--layout-topbar-height}}
      {{tok:Side padding|--layout-margin}}
      {{tok:Link height|--target-comfortable}}
      {{tok:Layer|--z-sticky}}
      {{tok:Brand font / link font|--text-h4|--text-label}}
      {{tok:Transition|--duration-fast|--ease-standard}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;header class="topbar"&gt;
  &lt;a class="topbar__brand" href="/"&gt;&lt;svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true" …&gt;…&lt;/svg&gt;HairPop&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;nav class="topbar__nav" id="primary-nav" aria-label="Primary"&gt;
    &lt;a class="nav-link" href="/" aria-current="page"&gt;Styles&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;a class="nav-link" href="/braiders"&gt;Braiders&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;a class="nav-link" href="/appointments"&gt;Appointments&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;a class="nav-link" href="/help"&gt;Help&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;/nav&gt;
  &lt;span class="topbar__spacer"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;a class="account-link" href="/notifications"&gt;Updates &lt;span class="badge badge--count"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="visually-hidden"&gt;, 2 unread&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon topbar__menu" type="button" aria-label="Menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="primary-nav"&gt;…&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;a class="account-link" href="/settings"&gt;Maya&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.topbar</code></td><td>Sticky 56px bar; flex row with <code>--space-3</code> gaps.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.topbar__brand</code></td><td>Brand link in the accent colour, 44px tall.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.topbar__nav</code></td><td>Primary links; hidden below 768px, flex from 768px.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.topbar__spacer</code></td><td>Pushes Updates and the account to the right.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.topbar__menu</code></td><td>Menu button; shown below 768px only.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.nav-link</code> + <code>aria-current="page"</code></td><td>Navigation link; current page gets the accent-subtle look.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.account-link</code></td><td>Right-hand utility link (Updates, account), 44px tall.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>aria-expanded</code> / <code>aria-controls</code></td><td>Menu button state and the id of the nav it opens.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>--topbar-bg</code></td><td>Component token for the bar background.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-state="hover|focus|active|current"</code></td><td>Documentation only: forces a link state.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <p>Extracted from the shell shared by every mock, notably:</p>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/style-gallery/default|Styles current}}
    {{mock:pages/matching-braiders/default|Braiders current}}
    {{mock:pages/my-appointments/default|Appointments current}}
    {{mock:pages/help/default|Help current}}
    {{mock:pages/notification-center/default|Updates destination}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: below 768px the mocks hide the primary nav with no menu button (system adds a disclosure menu button); the Updates link was labelled "Notifications, 2 unread", which does not contain its visible text (system appends hidden ", 2 unread" to the visible text); the count badge also carried its own <code>aria-label</code> inside the labelled link (removed); the brand used a "✦" text glyph (system uses the sparkle icon, <code>aria-hidden</code>); <code>.topbar</code> declared its gap twice (single <code>--space-3</code>); the account link used a <code>max-width</code> query for its phone size (rewritten mobile-first).</p>
</section>
